  "notes": [
    "Unbundling: a claim line whose code is a component_code of a bundle pair is a violation when another line of the same claim (same member and provider) with the pair's comprehensive_code has the same service_date, and the component line's own modifiers do not include that pair's exception_modifier. A modifier on the comprehensive line or on any other line does not help. A different modifier than the pair's exception_modifier does not help. Only the component line is the anomaly.",
    "Excess units: a line is a violation when its own units exceed the max_units of its code. Units are never added across lines. Codes not listed in unit_limits (visit codes, general procedure codes, bundle codes) have no unit maximum.",
    "Date anomaly: a line is a violation when its service_date is before the claim service_from or after the claim service_to. Dates equal to service_from or service_to are inside the period.",
    "A component code with no matching comprehensive code on the same date is not a violation."
  ]
